      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e `mount -t cpuset -ocpuset_v2_mode cgroup /dev/cpuset_tmp02`\n\nSo this is not what the patch will do.\n\n`mount -t cgroup -ocpuset,noprefix,cpuset_v2_mode cgroup /dev/cpuset_tmp02`\nis what it will do.\n\nThe problem is the `cpuset` filesystem type does not support `cpuset_v2_mode` until https://lore.kernel.org/all/20250416211752.945849-1-tjmercier@google.com/. So you cannot do `mount -t cpuset -ocpuset_v2_mode cgroup /dev/cpuset_tmp02` unless you have that kernel patch, which we can\u0027t guarantee all Android devices will have for a while.\n\n(Using `cpuset` with) the `cgroup` filesystem type and `cpuset_v2_mode` has been supported since 2017: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id\u003de1cba4b85daa71b710384d451ff6238d5e4d1ff6",
      "parentUuid": "34d7085c_e60c4fae",
