      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. The following patches mentioned by you have been contained in test image:\n     https://lore.kernel.org/all/20250416211752.945849-1-tjmercier@google.com/\n     https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id\u003de1cba4b85daa71b710384d451ff6238d5e4d1ff6\n\n2. I did new verification using \"mount -t cgroup -ocpuset,noprefix,cpuset_v2_mode cgroup /dev/cpuset_tmp02\", the following warning log still can be got:\n    [  349.141361] new mount options do not match the existing superblock, will be ignored\n    \n\n3. In my debug, when cpuset_parse_param() is called, it always returns from the following code:\n    opt \u003d fs_parse(fc, cpuset_fs_parameters, param, \u0026result);\n    if (opt \u003c 0)\n        return opt;\n\n\nthe following \"CGRP_ROOT_CPUSET_V2_MODE\" setting cannot be completed:\n    switch (opt) {\n    case Opt_cpuset_v2_mode:\n             ctx-\u003eflags |\u003d CGRP_ROOT_CPUSET_V2_MODE;\n             return 0;\n    }\n\nI don\u0027t know whether there is any other bug about the support of \"cpuset_v2_mode\".\nPlease consider continuing the review and merging this change. There have been quite a few reports and complaints about this issue in the market.",
